"""
Reads a Bunti code (Wolly.Bunti) out of a picture, as a camera gives it:
red, green and blue bytes of each pixel, row by row (docs/bunti-format.md).

A pixel is dark when the highest of its three values lies below the
threshold Otsu's method finds for them: black is dark, and the four colours
of the bases are not, each having one value near the top.  The finder
patterns are found by the runs dark, light, dark, light, dark of the widths
1 : 1 : 3 : 1 : 1 along the rows, checked down the column of their middle;
the corner pattern by 1 : 1 : 1 : 1 : 1.  The finder whose two others stand
at a right angle to it is the top left, the turn from it to the two
others tells top right from bottom left, so a code is read in any of its
four turns.  Their distance in cells gives the size, tried with its
neighbours; the three finders and the corner pattern give a perspective
transformation, and every cell is sampled in its middle and given the base
whose reference cell is nearest in colour.  The header must read and
name the size, Reed-Solomon and the CRC-32 must agree: a picture gives
its payload or an error, never other bytes.

Nothing here reads a file, the network or the clock.

    case decodeBuntiPixels(width, height, asSpan(&frame)) of
        when Right(right as payload: String) do ...
        when Left(left as error: BuntiError) do ...  -- NotFound, Damaged
    end case;
"""
import Standard.String (
    String
);
import Wolly.Bunti (
    BuntiError,
    BuntiCode
);

module Wolly.BuntiScan is
    """
    The cells of the code in width by height pixels of red, green and blue,
    row by row; Left NotFound when there is none, or pixels is not width
    * height * 3 bytes.  The header of the code is read already.
    No contract: it reads pixels as a parser reads text, and any width,
    height and length of pixels is answered, an impossible one with Left
    NotFound, never with a trap.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function readBuntiPixels(width: Index, height: Index, pixels: Span[Nat8, R]): Either[BuntiError, BuntiCode];

    """
    The payload of the code in the pixels: readBuntiPixels, then
    Wolly.Bunti.decodeBunti.
    No contract: as readBuntiPixels, any width, height and length of
    pixels is answered with an Either, never with a trap.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function decodeBuntiPixels(width: Index, height: Index, pixels: Span[Nat8, R]): Either[BuntiError, String];

    """
    The payload of the code in the PNG in data, read through Wolly.Image
    with at most maxPixels pixels.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function decodeBuntiPng(data: Span[Nat8, R], maxPixels: Index): Either[BuntiError, String]
        requires maxPixels > 0;
end module.
